{"task_id": "Mbpp/99", "solution": "```python\ndef decimal_to_binary(decimal_number: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a decimal integer to its binary string representation without leading zeros.\n    Handles non-negative integers; for 0, returns '0'.\n    \"\"\"\n    if decimal_number == 0:\n        return '0'\n\n    binary_string = \"\"\n    temp_number = decimal_number\n    while temp_number > 0:\n        binary_string = str(temp_number % 2) + binary_string\n        temp_number //= 2\n\n    return binary_string\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/100", "solution": "def next_smallest_palindrome(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the next smallest palindrome greater than the input integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    def reverse_number(num: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Reverses the digits of an integer.\n        \"\"\"\n        return int(str(num)[::-1])\n\n    def is_palindrome(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if an integer is a palindrome.\n        \"\"\"\n        return num == reverse_number(num)\n\n    def increment_and_find(start_num: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Increments a number and searches for the next palindrome.\n        \"\"\"\n        candidate = start_num + 1\n        while True:\n            if is_palindrome(candidate):\n                return candidate\n            candidate += 1\n\n    return increment_and_find(n)"}
