{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def _rotate_left(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs a single left rotation on a string.\n    Moves the first character to the end.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return s\n    return s[1:] + s[0]\n\ndef _binary_to_decimal(binary_str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a binary string to its decimal integer equivalent.\n    \"\"\"\n    return int(binary_str, 2)\n\ndef _is_odd(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given integer is an odd number.\n    Returns True if odd, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    return number % 2 != 0\n\ndef odd_Equivalent(binary_string, rotation_count):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts how many decimal values are odd when rotating a binary string.\n    The string is rotated `rotation_count` times, and each resulting decimal is checked.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_count = 0\n    current_string = binary_string\n\n    for _ in range(rotation_count):\n        decimal_val = _binary_to_decimal(current_string)\n        if _is_odd(decimal_val):\n            odd_count += 1\n        \n        current_string = _rotate_left(current_string)\n\n    return odd_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "def common_in_nested_lists(nested_lists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds common elements in a list of lists.\n    It returns a set of elements that appear in all sublists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nested_lists:\n        return set()\n\n    # Initialize common elements with the first sublist's elements\n    common_elements = set(nested_lists[0])\n\n    # Iterate through the remaining sublists and find intersections\n    for sublist in nested_lists[1:]:\n        common_elements = common_elements.intersection(set(sublist))\n        # If common_elements becomes empty, no further intersection is needed\n        if not common_elements:\n            break\n\n    return common_elements"}
