{"task_id": "Mbpp/138", "solution": "def is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a positive integer can be represented as a sum of distinct powers of two,\n    excluding the power 2^0 (which is 1).\n    \"\"\"\n    # A number can be represented as a sum of distinct powers of two where the\n    # exponent k > 0, if and only if the number is positive and even.\n    # This is because all powers 2^k for k > 0 are even, and their sum will be even.\n    # The least significant bit of such a number's binary representation must be 0.\n    if number <= 0:\n        return False\n    if number % 2 != 0:\n        return False\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "def zero_count(array: list[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the ratio of zeroes to non-zeroes in an array of integers.\n    Returns 0.0 if there are no non-zero elements to avoid division by zero.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_zeros = 0\n    num_non_zeros = 0\n\n    for x in array:\n        if x == 0:\n            num_zeros += 1\n        else:\n            num_non_zeros += 1\n\n    if num_non_zeros == 0:\n        return 0.0  # Handle division by zero case as specified in design context\n    else:\n        return float(num_zeros) / num_non_zeros"}
