{"task_id": "Mbpp/410", "solution": "def _validate_input(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates if the input is a non-empty list.\n    Raises TypeError if not a list, ValueError if empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(lst, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    if not lst:\n        raise ValueError(\"Empty list provided\")\n\ndef _filter_numeric_values(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Filters a list to include only integer and float values.\n    Returns a new list containing only numeric elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    numeric_values = []\n    for item in lst:\n        if isinstance(item, (int, float)):\n            numeric_values.append(item)\n    return numeric_values\n\ndef min_val(input_list: list) -> int or float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum numeric value in a heterogeneous list.\n    Filters out non-numeric values and handles edge cases.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_input(input_list)\n\n    filtered_numerics = _filter_numeric_values(input_list)\n\n    if not filtered_numerics:\n        raise ValueError(\"No numeric values found in the list.\")\n\n    return min(filtered_numerics)"}
