{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def shell_sort(array: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts an array using the Shell Sort algorithm.\n    It creates a copy of the array and sorts it in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n    sorted_array = list(array) # Create a copy to avoid modifying the original array.\n\n    def _generate_gap_sequence(length: int) -> list:\n        \"\"\"Generates a standard decreasing gap sequence for Shell sort.\"\"\"\n        gaps = []\n        gap = length // 2\n        while gap > 0:\n            gaps.append(gap)\n            gap //= 2\n        return gaps\n\n    def _insertion_sort_with_gap(arr: list, current_gap: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Performs gapped insertion sort on the array.\"\"\"\n        for i in range(current_gap, n):\n            current_value = arr[i]\n            position = i\n            # Shift elements that are greater than current_value to the right.\n            while position >= current_gap and arr[position - current_gap] > current_value:\n                arr[position] = arr[position - current_gap]\n                position -= current_gap\n            arr[position] = current_value\n\n    gaps = _generate_gap_sequence(n)\n\n    # Apply gapped insertion sort for each gap in the sequence.\n    for gap in gaps:\n        _insertion_sort_with_gap(sorted_array, gap)\n\n    return sorted_array"}
